From 75c7ad9ae682469dd0c8c87b0cecbd3f905c80d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:28:28 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] =?UTF-8?q?Add=20course=20folder=20generator=20(OBE=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=86=92=20Course=20folder)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Faculty upload course_information.xlsx and the course outline, download a
marks sheet with student IDs filled in, upload it filled, and get the whole
course file as a zip, built in the browser:

- CO-PO Mapping, Instructors and Schedule and CAR filled into copies of the
  department's Word files (src/assets/course-folder), plus a generated
  CO-PO Attainment Report
- CO-PO assessment marks workbook in the BME 211 layout with live formulas
  (theory: attendance, best-k CTs, TF sections, Q1/Q5 sub-part CO mapping;
  sessional: one column per assessment from the distribution of marks)
- assessment folders with highest / average / lowest students to upload,
  lecture-material folders, BUGS link and a generation log

Rules follow the dept policy: >= 40% student and cohort thresholds, PO% as the
mean of mapped COs, and a student absent in every item of a CO is left out
of that CO. New `sections` sheet in course_information gives the roll range.
Available on the OBE page and on each course's OBE tab. No database changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BE2UHP816kUcpU2VSMQzUY
